{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]They were all together in one place [G]when Pentecost had [D]come
Waiting for the promise as the Lord had told them, [G]every one
Then a [Bm]sound came from heaven like a [A]rushing, violent [G]wind
[Bm]And tongues as of fire came [A]down and rested on [G]each of them
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will [D]pour out my Spirit on all [G]flesh
Your sons and your daughters will prop[Bm]hesy
Your young men will see vi[A]sions
And your old men will dream [D]dreams
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
From every nation under heaven came [G]a crowd to hear the [D]sound
Each [Bm]one heard them in his own language, and amaze[G]ment spread around
Some mocked [Bm]them, full of new [A]wine, but Peter stood up [G]with the eleven
And raised [Bm]his voice to tell them [A]of the promise sent from heav[G]en
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
